Add `src/vite-env.d.ts` containing exactly:
```ts
/// <reference types="vite/client" />
interface ViteTypeOptions { strictImportMetaEnv: unknown }
interface ImportMetaEnv { readonly BASE_URL: string }
```
Declaring `strictImportMetaEnv` flips `ImportMetaEnvFallbackKey` to `never`, which removes the `any` index signature: unknown env keys then become compile errors and declared ones get real types. Adding a key later means declaring it in this one file. Risk: if any tooling in the build reads an undeclared `import.meta.env` key it will now fail to typecheck — which is the point, but check `vite build` once after landing.

