```
The `in` check narrows without an assertion and covers null, undefined and primitives in one line. errors.test.ts already exists — add two table rows for `toAiError(null)` and `toAiError(undefined)` asserting kind 'unknown'. Risk: none; behaviour is unchanged for every value that does not currently crash.

