findings.suggestedPatch:
Add one shim and route all five sites through it — e.g. `src/lib/id.ts`:
```ts
export function newId(): string {
  if (typeof crypto !== 'undefined' && typeof crypto.randomUUID === 'function') return crypto.randomUUID();
  const b = new Uint8Array(16);
  crypto.getRandomValues(b); // available in insecure contexts
  b[6] = (b[6]! & 0x0f) | 0x40; b[8] = (b[8]! & 0x3f) | 0x80;
  const h = [...b].map(x => x.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('');
  return `${h.slice(0,8)}-${h.slice(8,12)}-${h.slice(12,16)}-${h.slice(16,20)}-${h.slice(20)}`;
}
```
This is the spec's 'isolate the platform quirk in one shim with a strictly typed public face' pattern. `crypto.getRandomValues` is not secure-context-gated, so the fallback is still cryptographically sound. Risk: ids stay v4-shaped and opaque, so nothing downstream changes; keep the fallback branch covered by a unit test that stubs `crypto.randomUUID` to undefined.

